From: Peter Kamami <peterkamami496@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:08:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Document the SMARTTT connection settings in .env.example

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MKtx9SS2GuCYU7oVG3uhYj
---
 .env.example | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
index 9950609..e8a8190 100644
--- a/.env.example
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -85,9 +85,14 @@ ERP_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
 ERP_MAX_RETRIES=2
 
 # --- SMARTTT (university timetable) ---
-# Where a lecturer's units and each unit's registered-student count come from.
-# Leave SMARTTT_BASE_URL empty to switch the sync off.
-# SMARTTT_API_KEY must equal ATTENDANCE_API_KEY in SMARTTT's environment.
+# Where a lecturer's units, groups, rosters and registered-student counts come
+# from, and where a student's registration number is checked.
+# SMARTTT_BASE_URL is the SMARTTT backend root, no trailing slash, e.g.
+#   production: https://smarttt-backend-n44z.onrender.com
+#   local:      http://localhost:8000
+# Leave it empty to switch the SMARTTT connection off.
+# SMARTTT_API_KEY is sent in the X-API-Key header on every call. It must equal
+# ATTENDANCE_API_KEY in SMARTTT's environment; SMARTTT refuses anything else.
 SMARTTT_BASE_URL=
 SMARTTT_API_KEY=
 SMARTTT_LECTURER_UNITS_PATH=/api/v1/integrations/attendance/lecturer-units/
